WEBVTT

00:01.967 --> 00:03.677
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.761 --> 00:05.262
That's a satellite phone.

00:05.346 --> 00:06.889
From where did you take off?

00:06.972 --> 00:10.643
A freighter.
About 80 nautical miles west of here.

00:10.726 --> 00:12.634
I'm part of a search-and-recovery team.

00:12.728 --> 00:15.981
Ben is using one of the Dharma stations
to block all the signals.

00:16.065 --> 00:18.442
It's an underwater Dharma station.
We swim in.

00:18.526 --> 00:19.558
I'll do it.

00:19.652 --> 00:22.227
While I'm gone, don't worry about me.

00:22.863 --> 00:25.157
How long will it take you
to reach their camp?

00:25.241 --> 00:27.701
If I take my ten best
we can hit them by nightfall.

00:27.785 --> 00:30.996
If any of them are stupid enough
to get in your way, kill them.

00:32.707 --> 00:36.836
We camouflage the dynamite next to
the tents, target it from the tree line.

00:36.919 --> 00:39.588
When your people show up tomorrow
we'll be ready.

00:39.672 --> 00:43.290
- No, they're coming tonight!
- You lead everyone to the radio tower.

00:43.384 --> 00:46.137
Can't risk losing the chance
to contact Naomi's boat.

00:46.220 --> 00:48.295
Everything has to happen
at the same time.

00:48.389 --> 00:49.807
What I saw, Charlie,

00:49.890 --> 00:53.477
was Claire and her baby getting into
a helicopter that leaves this island.

00:53.561 --> 00:55.438
This time, you have to die.

00:55.521 --> 00:58.149
If you don't, there won't be any rescue.

01:05.448 --> 01:06.866
I'm alive!

01:28.012 --> 01:30.420
Would you put your seatback up, please?

01:31.515 --> 01:33.924
Would you fasten your seat belt, please?

01:34.518 --> 01:36.062
Excuse me. Excuse me.

01:37.063 --> 01:39.555
Can I get another one of those, please?

01:39.648 --> 01:42.141
I'm sorry, sir.
We'll be landing in 20 minutes.

01:42.234 --> 01:45.571
- Well, 20 minutes is a long time.
- How about a newspaper instead?

01:45.654 --> 01:47.948
And if you could
buckle your seat belt, sir?

01:48.824 --> 01:51.285
Please fasten your seat belt. Thank you.

02:00.544 --> 02:02.380
<i>Sorry about the bumps</i>, <i>folks.</i>

02:02.463 --> 02:05.508
<i>We're hitting warm air</i>
<i>as we descend into Los Angeles.</i>

02:05.591 --> 02:09.762
<i>Please keep those seat belts fastened.</i>
<i>We'll have you on the ground shortly.</i>

03:22.877 --> 03:27.590
<i>You've reached 310-555-0148.</i>

03:27.673 --> 03:29.550
<i>Please leave a message.</i>

03:29.633 --> 03:32.261
Hey. It's me.

03:34.263 --> 03:36.255
I...

03:38.976 --> 03:40.436
I just read...

04:51.215 --> 04:52.883
Oh, forgive me.

05:02.476 --> 05:05.896
Mom! Mom! Mom!

05:06.480 --> 05:07.982
- Help!
- Mom!

05:36.343 --> 05:37.970
You have everything you need?

05:38.054 --> 05:40.890
No. But I've made the best
out of what we have.

05:43.100 --> 05:46.604
- Bernard and Jin?
- They're both excellent shots.

05:46.687 --> 05:48.522
And highly motivated.

05:50.191 --> 05:52.766
The dynamite's in place. We won't miss.

05:53.611 --> 05:56.822
Jack, no matter what happens here,
I want you to keep moving.

05:56.906 --> 06:01.327
Keep moving for that radio tower.
Don't turn back for any reason.

06:02.411 --> 06:04.903
I'm willing to give my life
if it means rescue.

06:04.997 --> 06:09.543
But I am not giving it up for nothing.
You understand?

06:13.964 --> 06:17.499
Yeah. I understand.

06:22.515 --> 06:25.799
- Then, good luck.
- You too.

06:34.819 --> 06:39.240
If I'd help you with your SOS sign,
would you change your mind?

06:39.323 --> 06:42.243
- No, ma'am.
- Then I want you to say it again.

06:42.326 --> 06:44.453
- Rose...
- Say it, Bernard.

06:45.621 --> 06:48.833
I am a dentist. I am not Rambo.

06:48.916 --> 06:50.908
And don't you forget it.

07:07.643 --> 07:11.689
- Charlie's gonna be fine.
- Yeah. Of course he is.

07:22.992 --> 07:24.493
Jin...

07:34.754 --> 07:38.966
Because we have to go home.

07:56.525 --> 07:57.985
All right.

07:59.487 --> 08:01.072
Let's do it.

09:16.147 --> 09:18.858
Jack, can I ask you a question?

09:19.483 --> 09:20.568
Sure.

09:20.651 --> 09:23.904
What did you do for a living
before you became Moses?

09:24.864 --> 09:27.825
- I was a doctor.
- Right. 'Course you were.

09:27.908 --> 09:30.619
Well, I need your attention
for a minute, doctor.

09:32.997 --> 09:34.279
Is she OK?

09:35.958 --> 09:39.910
- Why wouldn't she be?
- Because none of your people trust her.

09:40.004 --> 09:41.589
No offence.

09:41.672 --> 09:44.081
- Catch up to me when you're done.
- Juliet...

09:44.175 --> 09:45.207
It's fine.

09:49.221 --> 09:51.463
I need to show you
how this gadget works,

09:51.557 --> 09:53.350
in case anything happens to me.

09:53.434 --> 09:55.644
You need to be able to call my boat.

09:56.604 --> 09:58.189
OK. Show me.

09:58.272 --> 10:00.733
It's actually simple. Turn her on here.

10:00.816 --> 10:03.527
This opens a direct channel
to the freighter.

10:03.611 --> 10:04.945
Give her a tap here,

10:05.029 --> 10:08.783
- wait for the beep and say hello.
- That's it?

10:08.866 --> 10:10.034
That's it.

10:10.117 --> 10:13.162
Once the rock star turns off
whatever's jamming us up,

10:13.245 --> 10:16.530
this red light will turn
a lovely shade of green.

10:16.624 --> 10:20.669
- That'll be any time now, yeah?
- Hopefully.

10:33.599 --> 10:35.351
Who are you?

10:36.644 --> 10:40.231
Look, if you tell us how
you got down here, we won't hurt you.

10:41.774 --> 10:44.443
I came in my invisible submarine.
Don't you see it?

10:45.569 --> 10:48.937
- Hey! Take it easy.
- Take it easy? He's one of them!

10:50.699 --> 10:54.703
Why are you here?
How did you find out about this station?

10:57.415 --> 10:58.958
Juliet told us.

11:00.418 --> 11:03.869
She's one of us now,
in case you hadn't heard.

11:04.839 --> 11:05.923
Stop.

11:08.134 --> 11:12.221
- We gotta call Ben.
- Yeah.

11:12.304 --> 11:14.379
Let's call Ben.

11:17.518 --> 11:19.019
Come on.

11:31.615 --> 11:33.743
<i>You're inside a room full of equipment.</i>

11:33.826 --> 11:37.246
There's a blinking yellow light
above a switch.

11:37.329 --> 11:41.114
<i>You flip the switch.</i>
<i>The light goes off.</i>

11:42.877 --> 11:44.670
And you drown.

11:53.054 --> 11:55.181
<i>Ben. Come in</i>, <i>Ben.</i>

11:56.849 --> 11:59.174
- Hello?
- <i>Ben. It's Bonnie.</i>

12:00.227 --> 12:02.553
<i>Ben</i>, <i>are you there?</i>

12:02.646 --> 12:04.190
<i>Can you hear me</i>, <i>Ben?</i>

12:06.776 --> 12:08.934
Why are you breaking radio silence?

12:09.028 --> 12:11.655
- One of them's down here.
- I'm sorry. What?

12:11.739 --> 12:15.409
<i>We've got him tied up</i>, <i>but he's here.</i>
<i>One of them swam down here.</i>

12:15.493 --> 12:17.901
- Who? Which one?
- He won't tell us.

12:17.995 --> 12:21.207
It's Charlie! Tell him I said hi!

12:21.290 --> 12:23.282
How did...?

12:23.376 --> 12:26.796
- <i>How does he know about the station?</i>
- He said Juliet told them.

12:34.720 --> 12:38.391
All right, sit tight.
Don't do anything. I'm sending help.

12:38.474 --> 12:42.144
Go to the Looking Glass and find out
what Charlie is doing down there.

12:42.228 --> 12:45.231
You told us the Looking Glass
was inoperable, flooded.

12:46.524 --> 12:47.806
I lied.

12:47.900 --> 12:50.569
Mikhail, I need you to go, now!

12:51.695 --> 12:52.947
I can be there by dawn.

12:54.365 --> 12:57.243
But if Juliet told them
about the Looking Glass,

12:57.326 --> 12:59.161
what else did she tell them?

13:06.210 --> 13:09.213
Ryan, come in. Ryan, are you there?

13:20.975 --> 13:22.966
- Your walkies all off?
- Yes, sir.

13:25.187 --> 13:26.731
Did you get a good look?

13:26.814 --> 13:30.766
The tents are marked with white coral.
Three of them. Juliet did her job.

13:30.860 --> 13:32.903
All right. Let's do this.

14:29.794 --> 14:31.785
It's empty!

14:31.879 --> 14:33.297
Get away from the tent!

14:36.675 --> 14:38.302
- It's a trap!
- Please, God.

14:38.386 --> 14:39.668
Get away from the...

14:42.056 --> 14:43.338
Move! Move!

14:45.518 --> 14:47.478
Tree line!

14:59.407 --> 15:02.368
I got your man! Drop your weapons!

15:12.712 --> 15:14.620
I got your man!

15:16.006 --> 15:17.550
It's over!

15:19.552 --> 15:22.388
Don't. Finger off the trigger.

15:30.980 --> 15:32.179
Was that gunfire?

15:32.273 --> 15:36.058
There were supposed
to be three explosions.

15:36.819 --> 15:38.446
- Yeah.
- There was.

15:43.576 --> 15:45.870
It didn't work.

15:51.000 --> 15:55.171
<i>Dr Leon to surgery.</i>
<i>Dr Leon to surgery.</i>

15:55.254 --> 15:58.466
- There ya go. Good as new.
- Thanks.

15:58.549 --> 16:00.707
The news people are waiting outside.

16:00.801 --> 16:04.086
- You being a hero, and all.
- Great.

16:06.098 --> 16:09.852
- The woman, how is she?
- She's been stabilised.

16:10.478 --> 16:13.439
- Thank God you were on that bridge.
- Right.

16:15.107 --> 16:17.735
Sorry, no visitors in the ER.

16:20.529 --> 16:23.282
It's OK. She...

16:24.450 --> 16:25.701
We used to be married.

16:27.286 --> 16:28.913
Come on in.

16:32.333 --> 16:33.918
What happened?

16:36.045 --> 16:40.789
It was a... a car accident.

16:41.675 --> 16:43.260
Are you OK?

16:45.805 --> 16:48.297
Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

16:49.767 --> 16:52.311
Are you drinking again?

16:54.522 --> 16:55.773
- No.
- Are you, Jack?

16:55.856 --> 16:57.108
No.

17:00.653 --> 17:02.613
Why did you come down here, Sarah?

17:03.864 --> 17:07.316
I'm still listed
as your emergency contact.

17:13.416 --> 17:17.169
What were you doing driving around
at 2:00 in the morning?

17:36.105 --> 17:38.649
Do you think maybe
you could give me a lift home?

17:43.195 --> 17:45.687
I don't think that would be appropriate.

17:49.410 --> 17:50.828
Well...

17:53.831 --> 17:56.375
...thanks for coming down, Sarah.

17:57.668 --> 17:59.336
Goodbye, Jack.

18:14.435 --> 18:16.927
Why were there only two explosions?

18:17.021 --> 18:18.856
They didn't have to blow the third.

18:18.939 --> 18:21.431
- But those gunshots...
- It's OK, Rose.

18:21.525 --> 18:23.235
- Do you believe that?
- Listen,

18:23.319 --> 18:26.363
they had no idea
that we were waiting for them.

18:26.447 --> 18:28.772
Sayid's with your husbands.
They're fine.

18:28.866 --> 18:30.618
They're a couple hours behind us.

18:30.701 --> 18:33.788
Then we should wait for them here.
You go on...

18:33.871 --> 18:35.154
No one gets left behind.

18:35.247 --> 18:39.335
If you say, "Live together, die alone,"
I'm gonna punch you in your face.

18:41.379 --> 18:45.247
Fair enough, Rose. Fair enough.

18:45.341 --> 18:49.387
But we have a plan.
And for all we know, it worked.

18:51.097 --> 18:53.766
It's gonna be OK.
Everything's gonna be all right.

18:55.643 --> 18:58.187
Let's just keep moving, OK?

19:09.156 --> 19:11.117
It's OK. Let's go.

19:18.999 --> 19:23.462
I'm gonna ask you this one more time.
Why are you here?

19:26.340 --> 19:30.177
I'm here to turn off
your jamming equipment.

19:30.261 --> 19:33.681
It's in there,
next to the flashing yellow light.

19:33.764 --> 19:36.934
- How do you know about that?
- I know because I know.

19:37.017 --> 19:40.354
Whatever you ladies do to me,
I'm going to turn it off.

19:40.438 --> 19:42.273
- You are?
- I most definitely am.

19:42.356 --> 19:45.891
- So, what's the code?
- What?

19:45.985 --> 19:49.071
Charlie, if you're gonna turn off
the jamming equipment,

19:49.155 --> 19:50.614
you're gonna need the code.

19:50.698 --> 19:52.992
And only three people know it:

19:53.075 --> 19:55.567
Me, her and Ben.

20:01.417 --> 20:04.545
Well, I guess I won't need the code,

20:04.628 --> 20:08.799
since this entire station's
gonna be flooded, anyway.

20:11.302 --> 20:12.970
I turn off your little jammer,

20:13.054 --> 20:15.379
and the helicopters
rescue all my friends.

20:15.473 --> 20:19.727
But if this station floods,
what happens to you?

20:23.814 --> 20:25.066
I die.

20:31.947 --> 20:33.824
- What?
- <i>They're all dead!</i>

20:33.908 --> 20:38.204
<i>Diane</i>, <i>Ivan</i>, <i>all of them</i>, <i>dead!</i>
<i>Shephard and his people</i>, <i>they're gone!</i>

20:38.287 --> 20:39.997
- Gone? Where?
- I don't know!

20:40.081 --> 20:42.708
Did you hear me?
They killed seven of our...

20:42.792 --> 20:45.586
Tom! Calm down
and tell him the good news.

20:45.669 --> 20:49.173
- What good news?
- We caught three of 'em.

20:49.256 --> 20:53.260
The ones that stayed to blow up the
tents. Ben, they knew we were coming.

20:53.344 --> 20:56.472
It was Juliet. She betrayed us.

20:56.555 --> 20:59.183
- What?
- Just figure out where she is, Tom!

21:00.393 --> 21:04.261
Get up. OK, junior.
Where the hell did...?

21:08.859 --> 21:10.986
- They're not talking.
- Who do you have?

21:11.070 --> 21:13.614
<i>Jarrah</i>, <i>Kwon and the dentist.</i>

21:13.697 --> 21:14.865
Shoot Kwon.

21:17.159 --> 21:18.869
- What?
- You want them to answer?

21:18.953 --> 21:20.413
Kill Kwon. Do it now.

21:22.039 --> 21:25.084
I don't know what that means,
but I'm sure it's lovely.

21:25.960 --> 21:27.837
- No! Wait! No!
- No! No talk!

21:27.920 --> 21:30.131
- Please!
- Talk to me. Nobody gets hurt.

21:30.214 --> 21:33.884
- Tell me where your people are.
- He's lying. He's going to kill us.

21:34.885 --> 21:37.044
Where are they?

21:41.892 --> 21:43.644
<i>Sayonara.</i>

21:44.395 --> 21:47.763
The radio tower.
They're hiking to a radio tower.

21:50.985 --> 21:55.156
- <i>Why in the hell are they going there?</i>
- <i>A woman parachuted here.</i>

21:55.823 --> 21:59.525
She has a satellite phone
and they're gonna call her ship.

21:59.618 --> 22:04.915
Juliet thought we were coming tomorrow.
So why were they waiting for us tonight?

22:04.999 --> 22:07.491
You heard him. How'd you know?

22:09.587 --> 22:14.300
A kid told us.
He came in a canoe and he warned us.

22:14.925 --> 22:16.469
What kid?

22:16.927 --> 22:18.888
Karl. He said his name was Karl.

22:19.764 --> 22:21.474
<i>You heard that</i>, <i>Ben?</i>

22:22.808 --> 22:24.060
<i>Ben?</i>

22:24.143 --> 22:25.561
I heard.

22:34.195 --> 22:36.186
What do you want us to do? Kill 'em?

22:38.699 --> 22:41.452
No. Not yet.

22:51.128 --> 22:52.880
We're going to the radio tower?

22:52.963 --> 22:54.715
Not we, Richard. Me.

22:54.799 --> 22:57.635
You're going to take everyone
to the Temple as planned.

22:57.718 --> 23:00.888
Now might not be the best time
to go tromping off on your own.

23:00.971 --> 23:02.056
And why not?

23:02.139 --> 23:03.766
People are asking questions.

23:03.849 --> 23:07.895
About leaving home, about
what happened to Locke, about Jacob.

23:09.105 --> 23:13.526
Not to mention the rumour that everyone
who went down to the beach is dead.

23:13.609 --> 23:15.069
They're not all dead.

23:21.033 --> 23:22.316
Where are you going?

23:22.410 --> 23:24.120
Hello, Alex.

23:24.787 --> 23:26.622
I asked where you were going.

23:26.705 --> 23:28.541
I thought I might go for a walk.

23:28.624 --> 23:31.752
See if I can't find Jack
and all his friends.

23:32.461 --> 23:34.369
I'm coming with you.

23:35.005 --> 23:37.299
- All right.
- What?

23:37.383 --> 23:39.093
I said, all right.

23:39.176 --> 23:41.220
In fact, I think it's a good idea.

23:42.346 --> 23:44.640
You do wanna see Karl again.
Don't you?

23:47.518 --> 23:50.187
Get your pack.
I'm leaving in ten minutes.

23:54.442 --> 23:56.934
There's 40 of them.
And you're alone.

23:57.027 --> 24:00.114
They're gonna do whatever it takes
to get off the island.

24:00.197 --> 24:02.950
What do you think's
gonna happen when you get there?

24:04.326 --> 24:06.036
I'm gonna talk them out of it.

24:35.066 --> 24:39.320
- Something's wrong.
- Lots of things are wrong, Kate.

24:39.403 --> 24:43.074
Jin, Bernard, Sayid,
they should've caught up to us by now.

24:43.616 --> 24:45.691
I wanna make sure they're all right.

24:45.785 --> 24:48.579
- 'Course you do.
- What's that supposed to mean?

24:48.662 --> 24:52.281
It means, Kate,
there's always someone to go back for.

24:53.250 --> 24:55.325
- What's the matter with you?
- Nothing.

24:56.587 --> 24:59.048
Why don't you just
tell me what happened?

25:05.971 --> 25:08.464
- What'd you do that for?
- To wake you up!

25:08.557 --> 25:12.812
Ever since you got that tape from Locke,
it's like you've been sleepwalking.

25:12.895 --> 25:15.106
You don't care about our friends? Fine.

25:15.189 --> 25:18.974
But it's like you don't care
about anything anymore.

25:19.068 --> 25:21.737
And since when
did you start calling me "Kate"?

25:26.325 --> 25:31.288
You know... they sent Juliet
to check out Sun.

25:34.709 --> 25:38.410
But she was there
to check and see if I'm pregnant too.

25:41.590 --> 25:43.426
Well, let's hope you're not.

25:58.441 --> 25:59.640
The light still red?

27:24.151 --> 27:26.112
Des! Des!

27:26.821 --> 27:29.740
Charlie! Bloody hell! You all right?

27:29.824 --> 27:32.868
Not for long, if you don't
get out of here. You have to hide!

27:32.952 --> 27:36.288
There's people in there! Quick! Hide!
Hide! Hide! Go, go, go!

27:36.956 --> 27:38.833
Who's he talking to?

27:39.709 --> 27:42.034
<i>Acting like you're stupid</i>

27:42.128 --> 27:44.036
<i>Stupid people</i>
<i>wearing expensive...</i>

27:44.130 --> 27:47.831
- Who were you talking to?
- I wasn't talking. I was singing.

27:47.925 --> 27:51.971
<i>You all</i>, <i>everybody</i>
<i>You all</i>, <i>everybody</i>

27:53.639 --> 27:57.393
<i>You all</i>, <i>everybody</i>
<i>You all</i>, <i>everybody...</i>

28:00.104 --> 28:02.648
- Shut up.
- Right. OK. You got it.

28:04.692 --> 28:06.026
Come on.

28:43.230 --> 28:44.482
Can I help you?

28:46.859 --> 28:48.486
Just checking her chart.

28:48.569 --> 28:51.614
I'm sorry, I'm Dr Hamill. Rob.
The new chief of surgery.

28:51.697 --> 28:54.273
- I don't think we've met yet.
- Jack Shephard.

28:54.366 --> 28:58.120
Dr Shephard, the hero. Twice over.

29:00.831 --> 29:02.114
Are you all right?

29:02.208 --> 29:05.576
After last night, I'm surprised
you'd even want to come in.

29:05.669 --> 29:09.757
Talk about right place, right time?
This woman is very lucky you were there.

29:09.840 --> 29:13.969
Then she wouldn't have a fractured back
that was impinging upon her spinal cord.

29:14.053 --> 29:17.640
I'd like to operate
first thing in the morning.

29:19.392 --> 29:22.103
- You want to operate?
- Yes.

29:22.186 --> 29:24.397
I'm sorry, Jack,
this isn't your patient.

29:24.480 --> 29:25.940
We are aware of the issues.

29:26.023 --> 29:29.110
Gary Nadler's doing
the surgery at 6:00am.

29:33.656 --> 29:37.524
With all due respect, Dr Hamill,
I'd rather do it myself.

29:39.495 --> 29:44.792
Last night you pulled this woman's
eight-year-old son out of a flaming car,

29:44.875 --> 29:46.544
then you went back for her.

29:48.754 --> 29:52.539
- I think you've done enough.
- I wanna do this surgery.

29:53.634 --> 29:58.097
Look, everything's under control here.
She'll be fine.

29:58.180 --> 30:02.049
Go home. Have a drink. You deserve it.

30:06.981 --> 30:08.858
The chart please, Jack.

30:17.324 --> 30:21.193
You call me.
I want to know what happens.

30:31.005 --> 30:33.966
<i>The 6th Street bridge</i>
<i>was shut down for several hours</i>,

30:34.050 --> 30:37.136
<i>in the wake of a fiery car accident</i>
<i>that left two injured.</i>

30:37.219 --> 30:40.473
<i>An unidentified 40-year-old woman</i>
<i>and her son.</i>

30:40.556 --> 30:42.965
<i>Fortunately for the two</i>,
<i>Dr Jack Shephard</i>

30:43.059 --> 30:46.677
<i>was near the scene</i>, <i>pulled the victims</i>
<i>from the burning wreckage</i>,

30:46.771 --> 30:49.940
<i>and treated them at the scene</i>
<i>until paramedics arrived.</i>

30:50.024 --> 30:53.360
<i>The victims were later transported</i>
<i>to St. Sebastian Hospital.</i>

30:53.444 --> 30:56.530
<i>Further details of their condition</i>
<i>have not been released.</i>

31:06.248 --> 31:09.377
- I'm going back.
- What?

31:09.460 --> 31:13.214
- I'm going back to the beach.
- No way. We keep moving.

31:13.297 --> 31:14.924
I ain't asking permission.

31:22.014 --> 31:23.766
Look, you got a job to do here.

31:23.849 --> 31:26.727
I ain't gonna stand
in your way of you doing it.

31:26.811 --> 31:28.396
But you sure don't need me.

31:28.479 --> 31:31.649
What do you think you're gonna get done,
alone and unarmed?

31:31.732 --> 31:34.026
- He won't be alone. I'll go with him.
- No.

31:38.239 --> 31:40.647
Twenty minutes ago,
you weren't even going,

31:40.741 --> 31:42.410
and now you're telling Jack...

31:42.493 --> 31:44.370
I didn't want to go with you.

31:46.997 --> 31:49.458
Sawyer, it's a suicide mission
without guns.

31:49.542 --> 31:52.086
I know where there are some guns.

31:52.169 --> 31:54.714
There's a hidden cache
a couple miles from here.

31:54.797 --> 31:57.758
I can take us back
to the beach on a route past it.

31:57.842 --> 32:00.000
Juliet, you don't have to do that.

32:00.553 --> 32:02.961
Yeah, Jack, I kinda do.

32:12.273 --> 32:13.983
Let's do this.

32:18.946 --> 32:22.366
- Don't do anything stupid.
- I won't if you won't.

32:32.710 --> 32:34.378
Don't wait up.

32:50.478 --> 32:54.774
- <i>The last of the ailing souls...</i>
- I told you to shut up!

32:54.857 --> 32:57.266
You know when you get a tune
stuck in your head?

32:57.359 --> 32:59.320
This song just started coming to me.

32:59.403 --> 33:00.602
It's almost finished.

33:00.696 --> 33:03.657
- I just need to find the bridge.
- Get the spear gun.

33:03.741 --> 33:05.785
- What? Why?
- Because I want it to hurt.

33:05.868 --> 33:09.236
- No. Ben said we have to...
- You don't wanna get it? I will.

33:09.789 --> 33:10.956
Bonnie!

33:12.708 --> 33:15.033
I'll shut up! I'll shut up!
I'll shut up!

33:19.757 --> 33:21.092
Mikhail?

33:23.469 --> 33:25.961
I thought you two
were on assignment in Canada.

33:30.267 --> 33:32.509
He made us promise not to tell anyone.

33:33.104 --> 33:35.648
- Hello again.
- Where is the other one?

33:36.107 --> 33:38.943
- What?
- This idiot swam down from a boat.

33:39.026 --> 33:42.895
I was just shooting at his friend.
He dove down here.

33:42.988 --> 33:45.230
- He's alone.
- Are you sure about that?

33:46.700 --> 33:49.026
Here's a better question
to ask, Cyclops.

33:49.120 --> 33:51.580
Why did your little friend Ben
tell you people

33:51.664 --> 33:54.417
that this entire station was flooded
when it isn't?

33:54.500 --> 33:58.754
Or why these two have been jamming
transmissions off the island?

33:58.838 --> 34:02.258
What? Is that true?

34:03.634 --> 34:05.793
- That's Ben.
- I'll get it.

34:12.226 --> 34:15.594
You have to understand.
Everything I did, I did for the island.

34:15.688 --> 34:18.972
The island told you it was necessary
to jam your own people?

34:19.066 --> 34:22.403
Yes, it did.
You've always been a loyalist, Mikhail.

34:22.486 --> 34:26.949
Now I'm asking you to trust me,
to trust Jacob, who told me to do this.

34:27.032 --> 34:29.577
Why would Jacob
ask you to lie to your own people?

34:29.660 --> 34:31.704
Because this island is under assault

34:31.787 --> 34:35.541
by forces stronger than anything
it's had to deal with in many years.

34:35.624 --> 34:39.159
And we are meant to protect it,
Mikhail, by any means necessary.

34:39.253 --> 34:42.788
The jamming was for everyone's security.

34:42.882 --> 34:45.885
We are in a serious situation here.

34:48.137 --> 34:50.347
So why not trust me?

34:50.431 --> 34:52.756
I made a mistake.

34:52.850 --> 34:56.020
I should have told you and I apologise.

34:58.564 --> 35:00.806
Mikhail? Are you still there?

35:05.613 --> 35:06.697
Yes.

35:09.492 --> 35:12.161
I need you to help me.

35:13.287 --> 35:17.041
I need you to help me clean up
this mess that I've made.

35:18.918 --> 35:21.243
I need you to kill Charlie.

35:22.213 --> 35:26.300
<i>Make sure that the jamming mechanism</i>
<i>continues to function at all costs.</i>

35:26.384 --> 35:29.918
We can't risk Greta and Bonnie
telling the others what we've done.

35:30.012 --> 35:32.723
So you'll have
to take care of them too.

35:36.894 --> 35:39.980
How do I know you didn't say
the same thing to them about me?

35:40.064 --> 35:44.777
Because if I had, Mikhail,
you'd already be dead.

36:08.259 --> 36:09.677
You OK?

36:11.429 --> 36:14.140
Yeah. I just got a rock in my shoe.

36:24.400 --> 36:25.860
He didn't mean it, you know.

36:28.028 --> 36:30.072
- What?
- Sawyer.

36:31.115 --> 36:34.702
When he said that he didn't want
you to come go him, he didn't mean it.

36:34.785 --> 36:37.277
If he didn't mean it, why'd he say it?

36:37.913 --> 36:40.291
He was trying to protect you.

36:43.252 --> 36:45.629
That's why I asked you
not to come back for me.

36:51.177 --> 36:55.723
Hey. Why are you sticking up for Sawyer?

36:55.806 --> 36:57.600
He'd never do it for you.

37:04.273 --> 37:06.108
Because I love you.

37:28.422 --> 37:30.914
When you pulled us out
of those polar bear cages

37:31.008 --> 37:33.333
and put us on the chain gang,

37:33.427 --> 37:36.055
what did you have us
breaking all those rocks for?

37:36.138 --> 37:39.266
- We were building a runway.
- A runway? For what?

37:40.184 --> 37:41.352
The aliens.

37:43.521 --> 37:46.857
I don't know what for.
Do you think they told me everything?

37:46.941 --> 37:48.932
Yeah, yeah. Whatever you say.

37:50.820 --> 37:54.104
- So you screwing Jack yet?
- No. Are you?

37:57.076 --> 38:00.079
- How far away are these guns?
- There aren't any guns.

38:01.664 --> 38:03.791
- What?
- I lied.

38:03.874 --> 38:07.211
- You lied?
- It was the only way he'd let us go.

38:13.926 --> 38:15.678
So why are you going back?

38:16.262 --> 38:17.596
Karma.

38:18.597 --> 38:21.173
Why are you going back, James?

38:21.642 --> 38:23.352
Hey!

38:25.146 --> 38:27.106
Hey, guys! Wait up!

38:29.108 --> 38:31.902
- What the hell do you want?
- I'm coming with you guys.

38:33.320 --> 38:34.780
No way, not a chance.

38:34.864 --> 38:38.565
Come on, I can help!
They're my friends too, man.

38:39.243 --> 38:41.287
Charlie wouldn't let me go with him.

38:41.370 --> 38:44.957
And Jack's too busy leading
to even talk to me.

38:46.083 --> 38:47.960
I just wanna help. Please?

38:50.546 --> 38:54.717
For God sakes, Hugo, look at you.
You're just gonna get in the way.

38:56.218 --> 38:58.544
You wanna get us killed?

39:01.849 --> 39:03.309
Come on.

39:17.948 --> 39:22.745
If we head north, we should get to them
before they reach the tower.

39:23.245 --> 39:24.747
Why did you let me come?

39:24.830 --> 39:28.282
I let you come because
I'm delivering you to your new family.

39:29.794 --> 39:33.130
I let you come
because you betrayed me, Alex.

39:33.214 --> 39:35.049
You locked Karl in a cage.

39:35.132 --> 39:37.676
You put him in a room
and tried to brainwash him.

39:38.719 --> 39:41.931
I didn't want him to get you pregnant.

39:42.014 --> 39:43.849
I suppose I overreacted.

39:46.227 --> 39:48.302
- We'd better get going.
- Ben...

39:49.397 --> 39:53.776
Why do you have to stop them?
Why won't you just let them leave?

39:56.695 --> 39:59.698
Because I can't, Alex.

41:39.965 --> 41:41.801
Don't, John.

41:48.808 --> 41:50.059
Put the gun down.

41:54.230 --> 41:55.429
Walt.

41:55.523 --> 41:57.681
Now, get up, John.

42:00.361 --> 42:05.157
He shot me, and I can't move my legs.

42:05.241 --> 42:08.942
You can move your legs.
Now, get out of the ditch, John.

42:10.287 --> 42:11.789
Why?

42:11.872 --> 42:14.750
Because you have work to do.
